# Cloudflare Workers Development Guide

Version: 1.1.0

Comprehensive guide for developing with Cloudflare Workers, Wrangler CLI, and related services in this project.

## Wrangler Configuration

### [wrangler.json](mdc:wrangler.json) Structure

The main configuration file for Cloudflare Workers:

```jsonc
{
  "name": "eddy",
  "main": "./src/worker/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2025-04-01",
  "compatibility_flags": [
    "nodejs_compat",
    "nodejs_compat_populate_process_env",
  ],
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  "upload_source_maps": true,
  "assets": { "not_found_handling": "single-page-application" },
}
```

### Environment Configuration

Two environments configured: `development` and `production`

**Development Environment:**

```jsonc
"env": {
  "development": {
    "vars": { "CLOUDFLARE_ENV": "dev" },
    "durable_objects": {
      "bindings": [
        { "name": "ChatAgent", "class_name": "ChatAgent" },
        { "name": "UserSettings", "class_name": "UserSettings" }
      ]
    },
    "migrations": [
      { "tag": "v0", "new_sqlite_classes": ["ChatAgent", "UserSettings"] }
    ],
    "d1_databases": [
      {
        "binding": "EDDY_AI_CHAT_DB",
        "database_name": "eddy-ai-chat-db-dev",
        "database_id": "52ed4e35-8ac0-464b-a569-fc788bdbac3c",
        "migrations_dir": "./src/worker/drizzle"
      }
    ],
    "ai": { "binding": "AI" }
  }
}
```

## Wrangler CLI Commands

### Development Commands

```bash
# Start local development server
npm run dev

# This runs: CLOUDFLARE_ENV=development vite

# Build and check bundle size
wrangler deploy --dry-run
```

### Deployment Commands

```bash
# Deploy to development
npm run deploy

# Deploy to production
npm run deploy:prod

# Build without deploying
npm run build
npm run build:prod
```

### Database Commands

```bash
# Generate migrations from schema
npm run db:generate

# Apply migrations locally
npm run db:migrate-local

# Apply migrations to dev environment
npm run db:migrate:dev

# Apply migrations to production
npm run db:migrate:prod

# Open database studio
npm run db:studio
```

### Type Generation

```bash
# Generate types for dev environment
npm run cf-typegen

# Generate types for prod environment
npm run cf-typegen:prod
```

## Worker Entry Point

### [src/worker/index.ts](mdc:src/worker/index.ts)

Main worker file structure:

```typescript
export { ChatAgent } from "./agents/chat-agent";
export { UserSettings } from "./durable_objects/user-settings";
import { trpcServer } from "@hono/trpc-server";
import { logger } from "hono/logger";
import { Hono } from "hono";
import { createContext } from "./trpc";
import { appRouter } from "./routes";
import { routeAgentRequest } from "agents";
import { auth } from "./lib/auth";
import { agentsMiddleware } from "hono-agents";

const app = new Hono<{ Bindings: Env }>();

// Middleware
app.use("*", logger());
app.use(
  "*",
  agentsMiddleware({
    options: {
      async onBeforeConnect(req) {
        const session = await auth.api.getSession({ headers: req.headers });
        if (!session) return new Response("Unauthorized", { status: 401 });
      },
      prefix: "agents",
    },
    onError: (error) => console.error(error),
  })
);

// Authentication routes
app.on(["POST", "GET"], "/api/auth/**", (c) => auth.handler(c.req.raw));

// Health check
app.get("/api/health", (c) => c.json({ status: true }, 200));

// tRPC routes
app.use("/trpc/*", async (c, next) =>
  trpcServer({
    router: appRouter,
    createContext: () => createContext(c),
  })(c, next)
);

// Agent routes
app.get("/agents/**", async (c) => {
  return (
    (await routeAgentRequest(c.req.raw, c.env)) ||
    new Response("Not found", { status: 404 })
  );
});

export default app;
```

## Bindings Configuration

### Environment Variables (Env interface)

Automatically generated in `worker-configuration.d.ts`:

```typescript
interface Env {
  // Database binding
  EDDY_AI_CHAT_DB: D1Database;

  // AI model binding
  AI: Ai;

  // Durable Object bindings
  ChatAgent: DurableObjectNamespace;
  UserSettings: DurableObjectNamespace;

  // Environment variables
  CLOUDFLARE_ENV: string;

  // API Keys (stored as secrets)
  GEMINI_API_KEY?: string;
  OPENAI_API_KEY?: string;
  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY?: string;
  XAI_API_KEY?: string;
  MISTRAL_API_KEY?: string;
  PERPLEXITY_API_KEY?: string;
  OPENROUTER_API_KEY?: string;
  DEEPSEEK_API_KEY?: string;
}
```

### Durable Objects

Agents are implemented as Durable Objects with persistence:

```jsonc
// In wrangler.json
"durable_objects": {
  "bindings": [
    { "name": "ChatAgent", "class_name": "ChatAgent" },
    { "name": "UserSettings", "class_name": "UserSettings" }
  ]
},
"migrations": [
  {
    "tag": "v0",
    "new_sqlite_classes": ["ChatAgent", "UserSettings"]
  }
]
```

### UserSettings Durable Object

Stores user API keys securely:

```typescript
import { DurableObject } from "cloudflare:workers";

export class UserSettings extends DurableObject<Env> {
  userApiKeys: Map<string, string> = new Map();
  private hasLoadedFromStorage = false;
  private static readonly STORAGE_KEY = "userApiKeys";

  async addOrUpdateUserApiKey(providerId: string, apiKey: string) {
    await this.ensureLoadedFromStorage();
    this.userApiKeys.set(providerId, apiKey);
    await this.ctx.storage.put(
      UserSettings.STORAGE_KEY,
      Object.fromEntries(this.userApiKeys)
    );
    return Object.fromEntries(this.userApiKeys);
  }

  async getUserApiKeyFromProviderId(providerId: string) {
    await this.ensureLoadedFromStorage();
    return this.userApiKeys.get(providerId) || "";
  }
}
```

### D1 Database

SQLite database binding configuration:

```typescript
// Accessing the database in your worker via Drizzle
import { drizzle } from "drizzle-orm/d1";
import { schema } from "./db/schema";

const db = drizzle(env.EDDY_AI_CHAT_DB, { schema });
const result = await db.select().from(schema.users);
```

### AI Binding

Access to Cloudflare AI models:

```typescript
// Using the AI binding (fallback when no user API key)
const response = await env.AI.run("@cf/meta/llama-2-7b-chat-int8", {
  messages: [{ role: "user", content: "Hello!" }],
});
```

## Development Best Practices

### 1. Environment Variables

Store sensitive data in environment files:

- `.dev.vars` - Local development secrets
- Use Wrangler secrets for production: `wrangler secret put SECRET_NAME`

Never commit these files to version control.

### 2. Type Safety

Generate types after configuration changes:

```bash
npm run cf-typegen
```

This creates type definitions for your bindings in `worker-configuration.d.ts`.

### 3. Local Development

```bash
# Start development with hot reloading
npm run dev

# This runs both:
# - Vite dev server for React app
# - Wrangler dev for Workers backend
```

### 4. Error Handling

Use proper error handling in your workers:

```typescript
app.onError((err, c) => {
  console.error("Unhandled error:", err);
  return c.json({ error: "Internal Server Error" }, 500);
});
```

### 5. Logging

Use structured logging for debugging:

```typescript
import { logger } from "hono/logger";

const app = new Hono();
app.use("*", logger());

// In your handlers
console.log("Processing request:", {
  url: request.url,
  method: request.method,
});
```

## Deployment Workflow

### 1. Development Deployment

```bash
npm run deploy
```

This:

- Builds the project with `CLOUDFLARE_ENV=development`
- Deploys to the development environment
- Uses dev database and environment variables

### 2. Production Deployment

```bash
npm run deploy:prod
```

This:

- Builds the project with `CLOUDFLARE_ENV=production`
- Deploys to the production environment
- Uses production database and environment variables

### 3. Database Migrations

Apply migrations after schema changes:

```bash
# Generate new migrations
npm run db:generate

# For development
npm run db:migrate:dev

# For production
npm run db:migrate:prod
```

## Monitoring and Debugging

### 1. Real-time Logs

View logs in development:

```bash
wrangler tail
```

### 2. Analytics

Access Worker analytics in the Cloudflare dashboard to monitor:

- Request volume
- Error rates
- Response times
- CPU usage

### 3. Observability

Observability is enabled in `wrangler.json`:

```jsonc
"observability": { "enabled": true }
```

This provides detailed metrics and tracing.

## Common Patterns

### 1. Request Routing with Hono

```typescript
const app = new Hono<{ Bindings: Env }>();

app.get("/api/users", async (c) => {
  const db = drizzle(c.env.EDDY_AI_CHAT_DB, { schema });
  const users = await db.select().from(schema.users);
  return c.json(users);
});
```

### 2. tRPC Integration

```typescript
import { router, publicProcedure, protectedProcedure } from "../trpc";

export const chats = router({
  getAll: protectedProcedure.query(async ({ ctx }) => {
    return ctx.db.select().from(schema.chats);
  }),
});
```

### 3. Agent Middleware with Authentication

```typescript
app.use(
  "*",
  agentsMiddleware({
    options: {
      async onBeforeConnect(req) {
        const session = await auth.api.getSession({ headers: req.headers });
        if (!session) return new Response("Unauthorized", { status: 401 });
      },
      prefix: "agents",
    },
    onError: (error) => console.error(error),
  })
);
```

### 4. Accessing Durable Objects

```typescript
// Get UserSettings for a specific user
const id = c.env.UserSettings.idFromName(userId);
const stub = c.env.UserSettings.get(id);
const apiKey = await stub.getUserApiKeyFromProviderId("openai");
```
